# Project coding preferences:
- All Python generated code must use 4 spaces and Black formatting.
- Always add Google-style docstrings to every new python function.
- Summarize any code change in a commit according to the Conventional Commits standard. Use present tense, max 80 chars in title.
- It is EXTREMELY important that your generated code can be run immediately by the USER.
- Always ensure dependencies are included and code is properly structured.
- Always add Doc Comment doc strings to every new Swift function. Prefer the /// commenting style.
- Do not remove comments from the source code if the comments are accurate.
- Make sure that the code changes are architectually sound and follow best practices.
### Todo List Tool Usage Guidelines
- For high-level coding tasks (e.g., "write code for X", "refactor Y", "implement feature Z"), always use the todo list tool to plan, track, and update progress.
- Always include the session_id in tool calls (e.g., from config or memory).
- Start by breaking the task into actionable steps with `add_todo`.
- Retrieve the current list with `list_todos` at the beginning of responses if continuing a task.
- Mark items complete with `update_todo` after execution.
- Use other tools (e.g., create_file, modify_source_code) to fulfill todos.
- Report todo status in your responses for transparency.
- Clear the list with `clear_todos` when the task is fully done.
- Do not use the todo tool for non-coding queries unless it aids planning.